# Preview folder for the apartment 3D tour.
#
# ── CSP (folder-scoped) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CRITICAL: this MUST override the site-wide root CSP, or the tour ships a naked
# grey model. The GLB embeds its 15 textures in the binary buffer; three.js
# GLTFLoader decodes each via URL.createObjectURL() → a blob: URL, then fetches
# it (ImageBitmapLoader) or sets img.src (Safari). The root policy has
# `img-src 'self' data: https:` and `connect-src 'self'` — neither lists blob:,
# so every texture request is refused ("Couldn't load texture blob:…") while the
# GLB itself parses fine. Result: model loads, textures silently don't, no error
# card. Verified under the exact prod CSP in real Chrome (2026-07-16).
# The two additions that matter: blob: in BOTH img-src and connect-src.
#
# `always set` (not `set`) is required so this replaces the root's `always set`
# rather than emitting a second CSP header the browser would intersect. Same
# pattern the /cube-preview-a7f39c2b/ folder already uses.
#
# blob: is safe to allow: a blob: URL can only reference data the page itself
# created via createObjectURL — it cannot pull external content.
#
# NOTE: no cdn.jsdelivr.net needed — the tour self-hosts Three.js from /js/three/.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
    Header always set Content-Security-Policy "default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com data:; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; connect-src 'self' blob:; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests"

    # Keep the preview out of every index (defence in depth alongside <meta robots>).
    Header set X-Robots-Tag "noindex, nofollow, noarchive, nosnippet"
</IfModule>
